# Modern Trivia — Agent Rules

> Read `CLAUDE.md` for full context. This file mirrors the key rules for Cursor-based agents.

## ⚠️ Current Priority: Professionalise (No New Features)

Feature development is paused. Focus on DevOps, security, and operational maturity only. All DevOps work is tracked under STE-66 in Linear.

## DevOps & Quality

### Git Workflow
- Branch naming: `feature/STE-XX-description` or `fix/STE-XX-description`
- Never push directly to `main` — use pull requests.
- CI must pass before merging.
- Do NOT use `--no-verify` to skip pre-commit hooks.

### Secrets
- **Never commit `.env` files or API keys.** A security incident has already occurred from this.
- Use `.env.example` as a template. Production secrets go in Replit Secrets.
- If you find hardcoded secrets in the codebase, stop and flag immediately.

### Testing & Linting (being set up)
- Run `npm run check` (type-check) before committing.
- Run `npm test` before committing (once available).
- Run `npm run lint` before committing (once available).
- New code must include tests.

### Multi-Agent Codebase
This repo is worked on by Claude Code Desktop, Claude Code Web, Replit Codex, and Antigravity. All agents follow the same rules. Pre-commit hooks and CI enforce standards regardless of agent.

## Trivia Content QA Specialist

Read `docs/guides/qa_instructions.md` for complete QA guidelines.

### Key Files
- Question database: `client/src/lib/questions.json`
- Full instructions: `docs/guides/qa_instructions.md`
- Editorial rules: `CONTENT_STRATEGY.md`

### Documentation Standards
- **Epics:** `docs/epics/EPIC-XX_slug_name.md`
- **Features:** `docs/feature_specs/FT-XX_slug_name.md`
- **Guides:** `docs/guides/topic_name.md`
- **Roadmap:** Always update `docs/PRODUCT_ROADMAP.md` with new items.

### Editorial Compliance
- GlobalEh must NOT be US-centric (no US state capitals, US-only history)
- FreshPrints must be from last 3 months — flag stale content
- Verify celebrity nationality before applying regional tags

### Data Integrity
- Required fields: id, category, difficulty, question, answer, explanation, tags
- Tags must include: regional tag (CA/US/Global), category, pillar
- Answers must work with 80% fuzzy matching

### Commit Format
`type(scope): description`
- fix(content): correct factual error in q128
- fix(devops): resolve CI lint failure
- feat(devops): add Vitest configuration

## When Uncertain
Flag for human review. Preserve original if unsure. Ask one clarifying question at a time.
